# i18n Execution Changes Log — Persistent Controller, Dictionaries, Profile Switcher

Resumed the i18n sprint after Task 1 (`AppLanguage`). Each task followed the TDD
loop (tests → implementation → targeted tests → backlog check-off → commit),
concluding with a full `fvm flutter analyze` and full `fvm flutter test`. All work
committed to `main`; verification used the pinned FVM SDK (Flutter 3.29.0).

## Task 2: Persistent Language Controller
- `lib/core/data/language_repository.dart` — narrow `LanguageRepository`
  contract (`get()` / `save(language)`), so persistence can change without
  touching the controller.
- `lib/core/data/local_language_repository.dart` — SQLite-backed implementation
  storing the ISO code under the `app_settings` `language` key; unknown values
  resolve to `null`.
- `lib/core/mocks/mock_language_repository.dart` — in-memory implementation for
  dev/test flavors.
- `lib/core/state/language_controller.dart` — `ChangeNotifier` with `language`,
  `locale`, `isLoaded`, `restore()` (hydrates the persisted choice, falls back to
  English) and `setLanguage()` (notifies immediately then persists; same-language
  set is a no-op).
- `lib/core/database/database_helper.dart` — schema `10→11`; new generic
  `app_settings(setting_key PK, setting_value)` table created in `_onCreate` and
  the `oldVersion < 11` upgrade path, plus `getSetting`/`upsertSetting`.
- Tests: `test/i18n/language_controller_test.dart`,
  `test/data/local_language_repository_test.dart`.

## Task 3: Translation Dictionaries
- `lib/core/domain/i18n/app_strings.dart` — typed `AppStrings` contract; every
  user-facing string is a getter, so adding a language is a compile-checked
  implementation and business logic never references a language directly.
  `AppStrings.of(language)` resolves the dictionary.
- `english_strings.dart` / `spanish_strings.dart` — full implementations covering
  navigation, screen headers, common actions/dialogs and quick-add labels.
- `localization_scope.dart` — `InheritedWidget` exposing the active language /
  dictionary; `stringsOf(context)` creates an inherited dependency so a language
  change rebuilds dependents in place, with a safe English fallback when no scope
  is present.
- Wired into the live UI: `BottomNavBar` labels and the `NutritionPage`
  header + quick-add button labels now resolve from the scope (quick-adds are
  localized by canonical name so logged `FoodEntry` names stay stable).
- Tests: `test/i18n/app_strings_test.dart` (contract completeness, en/es lookups,
  scope fallback and rebuild-on-change).

## Task 4: Settings / Profile Language Switcher UI
- `lib/ui/molecules/language_switcher.dart` — reactive switcher: one
  `OutlinedButton` chip per `AppLanguage.supported` (`language_option_en`,
  `language_option_es`), selected state highlighted, calling
  `LanguageController.setLanguage` for instant switching.
- `lib/ui/pages/profile_page.dart` — renders the switcher when a
  `LanguageController` is provided; the title is localized.
- `lib/ui/pages/main_shell_page.dart` — accepts and forwards an optional
  `languageController` to the Profile tab.
- `lib/app.dart` — creates the `LanguageController` (SQLite or mock repository),
  restores it at startup, and wraps the shell in a `ListenableBuilder` +
  `LocalizationScope` so switching rebuilds the whole app.
- Tests: `test/features/i18n_language_switcher_test.dart` (hidden without a
  controller, both options listed, instant Spanish refresh, persistence and
  restore on relaunch).

